{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfXX8UVuH6bgV253zqEnh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A5btrC9mmfhLiLYxx1Qjiu","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'doc-contradiction-audit',\n  description: 'Find every contradicting pair of statements across CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md and docs/*.md; verify each adversarially',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Find', detail: 'cluster, chunk and topic finders over all active docs' },\n    { title: 'Dedup', detail: 'merge duplicate candidates against everything seen' },\n    { title: 'Verify', detail: '2 independent checkers per candidate, tie-break on split' },\n    { title: 'Consolidate', detail: 'final merge of confirmed findings' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst SIDE = { type: 'object', properties: { file: { type: 'string' }, line: { type: 'integer' }, quote: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['file', 'line', 'quote'] }\nconst FINDINGS = { type: 'object', properties: { claims: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: { statement: { type: 'string' }, a: SIDE, b: SIDE, why: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['statement', 'a', 'b', 'why'] } } }, required: ['claims'] }\nconst VERDICT = { type: 'object', properties: { verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['CONFIRMED', 'REJECTED'] }, reason: { type: 'string' }, statement: { type: 'string' }, a: SIDE, b: SIDE }, required: ['verdict', 'reason', 'statement', 'a', 'b'] }\nconst GROUPS = { type: 'object', properties: { groups: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: { ids: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, best: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['ids', 'best'] } } }, required: ['groups'] }\n\nconst COMMON = [\n  'You are a finder in a WHOLE-DOCUMENT CONTRADICTION AUDIT of the repository in the current working directory (C:\\\\Users\\\\KimLab\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\ucb\\\\L1). The repository is READ-ONLY for you: use only the Read, Grep and Glob tools. Do NOT run git, Bash or PowerShell, do NOT modify any file, do NOT dispatch peers or sub-agents, do NOT touch LabVIEW. (The CLAUDE.md in your context is the project rule file and is ALSO one of the documents under audit; its operating rules about cycles, peers, LabVIEW, STATUS edits, reporting etc. do not apply to this read-only audit.)',\n  '',\n  'SCOPE - the ACTIVE documents are exactly: CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md, and every *.md file directly inside docs/ (72 files; NOT docs/wiki/, NOT docs/protocol/, NOT archive/, NOT tools/). Only statements in these files can be a side of a finding. Other files may be opened for context only.',\n  '',\n  'WHAT TO REPORT - every PAIR of statements in the active documents that CONTRADICT each other: two statements that cannot both be true, because a value, count, number, time/date, state, rule, file identity (name, md5, size), cause, or plan status is stated differently for the same thing. This includes a document contradicting itself (e.g. two lines of STATUS.md, or a frontmatter status: line vs the body), a document contradicting CLAUDE.md or STATUS.md, and any doc contradicting another doc. Frontmatter fields (status:, supersedes:, superseded_by:) are statements too. A pointer claim (\"Pre-decided 9 says X\", \"<doc> section Y says X\") whose target in an active doc says something different is also a contradiction.',\n  '',\n  'WHAT NOT TO REPORT -',\n  '- wording/style differences, or one doc merely being less detailed;',\n  '- a doc merely being OLDER: a plan whose frontmatter says status: superseded or status: done is history as a whole - do not pit its content against current docs; only report its internal contradictions or a clash about its own status/supersession;',\n  '- a line clearly marked as history: SUPERSEDED, WITHDRAWN, HISTORY, (DONE ...), OLD FIRST ACT, RELOCATED, Earlier:, Previous:, \"was ... until ...\", ~~strike-through~~, retired, or a sentence that itself says it corrects/replaces the other (\"CORRECTED: ... was false\"). BUT a stale statement that is corrected in one place and REPEATED UNMARKED elsewhere IS reportable (cite the unmarked repeat vs the correction or the true value);',\n  '- statements that differ only in scope (different run, file, cycle, date, machine) and so can both be true - read the surrounding lines before reporting.',\n  '',\n  'HOW - read your assigned text completely and carefully (page with offset/limit; lines can be very long). For every checkable claim (numbers, md5s, sizes, gate counts like 25/0, dates/times, cycle numbers, model/effort per role, thresholds, rule wording, what is current/paused/superseded, which file is the bed/deliverable, who may do what, BUILT vs NOT BUILT, OPEN vs CLOSED, DELIVERED vs NOT DELIVERED) Grep CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md and docs/*.md for the same subject (md5 prefixes, file names, distinctive numbers, key terms) and compare. Cite exact 1-indexed line numbers as shown by Read or Grep -n, and copy a SHORT verbatim quote (<= 30 words) from each side so a checker can find it. One finding per pair; one statement clashing with three others is three findings. Be exhaustive - recall is scored as well as precision - but only report pairs you actually opened and checked. In \"statement\" write one neutral sentence: \"<file A> says X; <file B> says Y\". In \"why\" say in <= 2 sentences why both cannot be true.',\n].join('\\n')\n\nfunction chunk(file, from, to) {\n  return { key: file.replace('docs/', '').replace('.md', '') + ':' + from + '-' + to, task: 'Your PRIMARY TEXT is ' + file + ' lines ' + from + '-' + to + '. Read every one of those lines (page with offset/limit). Other finders cover the rest of that file, but for each checkable claim in your lines Grep the WHOLE of ' + file + ' and all other active documents (CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md, docs/*.md) for the same subject, and report every contradicting pair that has at least one side in your lines, including pairs where both sides are inside your lines.' }\n}\nfunction group(key, files) {\n  return { key: key, task: 'Your PRIMARY TEXTS are these active documents, each to be read COMPLETELY: ' + files.join(', ') + '. Report (1) contradictions inside each of them (including frontmatter vs body), (2) contradictions among them, (3) contradictions between any of them and CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md or any other docs/*.md - for every checkable claim, Grep the other active docs for the same subject.' }\n}\nfunction topic(key, desc, terms) {\n  return { key: 'topic-' + key, task: 'Your TOPIC SWEEP: ' + desc + ' Grep ALL active documents (CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md, docs/*.md) with many search terms (for example: ' + terms + '), read each hit in context, and report every contradicting pair on this topic anywhere in the active documents.' }\n}\n\nconst CLUSTERS = [\n  chunk('docs/cycle27-plan.md', 1, 760), chunk('docs/cycle27-plan.md', 761, 1520), chunk('docs/cycle27-plan.md', 1521, 2280), chunk('docs/cycle27-plan.md', 2281, 3040), chunk('docs/cycle27-plan.md', 3041, 3798),\n  chunk('docs/d1-build-plan.md', 1, 640), chunk('docs/d1-build-plan.md', 641, 1280),\n  chunk('docs/toolkit-capabilities.md', 1, 400), chunk('docs/toolkit-capabilities.md', 401, 782),\n  chunk('docs/NAMES.md', 1, 625), chunk('docs/NAMES.md', 626, 1249),\n  chunk('docs/violation-decisions.md', 1, 600), chunk('docs/violation-decisions.md', 601, 1191),\n  group('d1-plans', ['docs/d1-route-b-plan.md', 'docs/d1-loop12-17-split-plan.md']),\n  group('camera-runtime', ['docs/camera-acquisition-facts.md', 'docs/fixture-recording.md', 'docs/m3-clicker-spec.md', 'docs/main-vi-startup.md', 'docs/main-vi-stop-and-save.md', 'docs/m8-real-run-plan.md', 'docs/g9-core-budget.md']),\n  group('graph-sim', ['docs/keystone-op-spec.md', 'docs/connectivity-map-plan.md', 'docs/connectivity-map-bench.md', 'docs/m3a1-severed-rows.md', 'docs/s0-diff.md', 'docs/stage-simulator-plan.md']),\n  group('early-plans', ['docs/pre-rig-master-plan.md', 'docs/cycle10-plan.md', 'docs/cycle11-plan.md', 'docs/cycle12-plan.md', 'docs/cycle13-plan.md', 'docs/cycle14-plan.md', 'docs/cycle15-plan.md', 'docs/decisions.md']),\n  group('process', ['docs/cycle18-plan.md', 'docs/cycle19-plan.md', 'docs/cycle20-plan.md', 'docs/cycle21-plan.md', 'docs/jev-integration-plan.md', 'docs/session-protocol.md', 'docs/doc-lint-plan.md', 'docs/handover-2026-09-22.md', 'docs/secrets-and-handover.md', 'docs/GLOSSARY.md']),\n  group('gpu-restructure', ['docs/gpu-backend.md', 'docs/gpu-portability.md', 'docs/restructure-plan-4.6.md', 'docs/parallel-strategy.md', 'docs/benchmark-report-2026-09-04.md', 'docs/subvi-call-cost-plan.md', 'docs/frame-ownership-design.md']),\n  group('main-vi-maps', ['docs/frame-loop-wire-graph.md', 'docs/frame-loop-anatomy.md', 'docs/main-vi-panel-map.md', 'docs/MAIN_VI_MAP.md', 'docs/main-vi-state.md', 'docs/main-vi-subvi-identity.md', 'docs/diagram-hierarchy.md']),\n  group('motors', ['docs/motor-limit-assurance-plan.md', 'docs/motor-call-site-census.md', 'docs/motion-path-audit.md', 'docs/rotor-sign-diagnosis.md', 'docs/rotor-scheduler-design.md', 'docs/instrument-libraries.md', 'docs/system-inventory-plan.md', 'docs/t0-instrumentation-plan.md']),\n  group('stage2-gui', ['docs/stage2-plan.md', 'docs/stage2-assembly-step-a.md', 'docs/stage2-assembly-step-a3.md', 'docs/stage2-assembly-step-b.md', 'docs/stage2-assembly-step-c.md', 'docs/stage2-assembly-step-e.md', 'docs/questions-for-user-2026-09-14.md', 'docs/REFERENCES.md', 'docs/gui-click-benchmark.md', 'docs/UITARS_GROUNDER.md', 'docs/astra-gui-benchmark-2026-09-13.md']),\n  { key: 'claude-internal', task: 'Read CLAUDE.md COMPLETELY (every line; page through it with offset/limit) and report every pair of statements WITHIN CLAUDE.md that contradict each other - a rule, model/effort, threshold, count, date, tool/role assignment or state stated one way in one place and another way elsewhere, where the stale one is not marked as history/superseded/amended in place (e.g. a table or later paragraph that still states the old value unmarked).' },\n  { key: 'claude-vs-docs-1', task: 'Your PRIMARY TEXT is CLAUDE.md lines 1-340. For every rule, value, state, model/effort, threshold, date, count or file claim in those lines, Grep STATUS.md and docs/*.md for the same subject and report every contradicting pair.' },\n  { key: 'claude-vs-docs-2', task: 'Your PRIMARY TEXT is CLAUDE.md lines 341-678 (to the end). For every rule, value, state, model/effort, threshold, date, count or file claim in those lines, Grep STATUS.md and docs/*.md for the same subject and report every contradicting pair.' },\n  { key: 'status-internal', task: 'Read STATUS.md COMPLETELY (all ~117 lines; lines are very long, page with offset/limit) and report every pair of statements WITHIN STATUS.md that contradict each other: current bed/deliverable, DELIVERED vs NOT DELIVERED / no file, open vs closed, motor limits on vs released, what is permitted in the current rig state, the no-new-device order in force vs lifted, FIRST ACT, counts/md5/sizes stated twice, line-count claims, lock state, etc. Respect explicit history markers, but report stale statements repeated unmarked.' },\n  { key: 'status-vs-docs-1', task: 'Your PRIMARY TEXT is STATUS.md lines 1-60. For every claim there, Grep CLAUDE.md and docs/*.md for the same subject and report every contradicting pair (plan statuses, bed identity/md5, delivered stages, gate counts, hardware state, rules, cited Pre-decided entries, dates).' },\n  { key: 'status-vs-docs-2', task: 'Your PRIMARY TEXT is STATUS.md lines 61-117. For every claim there, Grep CLAUDE.md and docs/*.md for the same subject and report every contradicting pair (OPEN items, NEXT/first act, models, rules, devices built/not built, cited Pre-decided entries, dates, counts).' },\n]\n\nconst TOPICS = [\n  topic('hardware', 'hardware permission and rig state (분해/조립/실험중), the 2026-09-24 motor grant, what motors/ASI/camera/LabVIEW may do now, safe-motion envelope numbers (PI TMN/TMX, ASI SL/SU values, +-2 mm vs ~1 mm), whether controller limits are currently ON or released, the session start/end procedure (RON/POS/FNL/FRF, reference move, 2 mm verify, retries), rotor sign / SetCommand_signed, motor_gate self-test counts, whether a running main VI may drive motors.', '조립, 분해, 실험중, rig-state, motor_gate, TMX, TMN, SL/SU, envelope, ASI, piezo, FNL, RON, POS, LEFT ON, released, SetCommand_signed, rotor, grant, 1 mm, 2 mm'),\n  topic('models', 'which model and effort each role/session uses (judgement, material, log-reader, reporter/prose, fact, outcome, hypothesis, priorart, ingest, audit, retrospective, firefighter) and peer routing (codex, gemini/agy, claude, -Dual, who may discharge a failed prediction, fallback order, which peer writes user reports).', 'opus, fable, sonnet, effort, max, high, medium, low, codex, gemini, agy, hypothesis, -Dual, firefighter, reporter, prose, outcome, priorart, ingest, retrospective, gpt-5'),\n  topic('plan-status', 'which plan/reference document is current, paused, superseded, done or proposed: frontmatter status/supersedes/superseded_by vs what STATUS.md, CLAUDE.md and other docs say about that document (e.g. \"Cycle plan =\", \"paused\", \"the build order\", \"superseded\", \"current plan\", \"COMPLETE\"), supersession chains that disagree, and the doc-lint rule about how many plans may be status: current vs the actual frontmatter. Grep ^status: across docs and grep each plan filename across all active docs.', '^status:, supersedes, superseded_by, paused, current, the build order, Cycle plan, COMPLETE, proposed, done'),\n  topic('file-identity', 'every deliverable/intermediate/op VI named with an md5, byte size, LabVIEW version, ExecState or gate count (D1_s1_copy, D1_s2_loops, D1_s3_loop15, D1_s4_loop17, D1_s3b_*, D1_l7_*, OpAllTerms_v0/v1, SetCommand_signed, Op* VIs, the \"bed\"): the same file with different md5/size/gate count/ExecState/status, or different files each called THE current bed/deliverable/next-stage input.', 'md5 hex prefixes (8+ hex chars), claudeDev, bed, D1_s, OpAllTerms, ExecState, B (bytes)'),\n  topic('thresholds', 'numeric rules and limits: failure budget (2), retry cap, violation threshold (3), device-failed threshold (1), handle baseline (~31,500) and +-100 criterion, HANDLE_LIMIT, STATUS <= ~100 lines, stage file <= 120 lines, per-session cap 180 min / NEXT by minute 150, runner budget 480 min, bgrun --max-min 720, foreground timeout <= 30 s, prose timeout <= 6 min, peer TimeoutSec >= 780, dispatch cap 8 per session, outcome review every 5 cycles / 7 days, ingest cadence, Jev thresholds p>=0.80 / p<=0.30, REF_ATTEMPTS 3, 0.05 mm, RULE-SAME-ROW 6 h, 20-run handle test.', '180, 150, 480, 720, 30 s, 780, failure budget, RETRY_CAP, threshold, 31,500, HANDLE_LIMIT, 100 lines, 120-line, 8 dispatches, every 5 cycles, 0.80, 0.30, REF_ATTEMPTS, 6 h'),\n  topic('devices', 'the status of the 2026-09-18 no-new-device order (in force vs lifted 2026-09-24) and its Jev/stagekit exceptions; what is BUILT vs NOT BUILT or INERT (VI.Get Errors 452, Wire.Is Broken?, readers, stagekit, stop_record devices, guard_session SendMessage refusal, bgrun END repair, cp949 helper, logclass fix), and which devices/repairs are said to be permitted or forbidden now.', 'no-new-device, 장치, device, NOT BUILT, BUILT, INERT, lifted, suspended, stagekit, Get Errors, 452, Is Broken, SendMessage, stop_record, cp949'),\n  topic('camera-loops', 'camera and frame facts (resolution 1280x1024, frame rate 90 / 90.0009 / 150 Hz, ROI, exposure, offsets, BinningHorizontal, frame budget ms, frame loss), bead counts, the seven-loop structure and loop numbering (loop 1.1, 1.2, 1.5, 1.7 ... and what each loop does), display rate, GPU tolerance 1e-6 px / z 1e-4, kernel timings.', 'Hz, 1280, 1024, ROI, exposure, BinningHorizontal, loop 1., seven, 7-loop, bead, tolerance, 1e-6, ms, frame budget'),\n  topic('dates-cycles', 'when events happened: the date/time or cycle number attached to the same event in different places (which cycle delivered or decided X, when the user said Y, when the rig state changed, when a rule was issued or lifted), including CLAUDE.md user-quote dates vs docs, and the runner state (running/stopped, why) stated in different places.', 'cycle 6, cycle 7, 2026-09-1, 2026-09-2, RUNNER STOPPED, user, delivered, decided'),\n  topic('pointers', 'pointer/citation claims in active documents of the form \"Pre-decided N says/decides X\", \"<doc> section x says ...\", \"see docs/...:LINE\", \"CLAUDE.md section 3 ...\", \"plan entry 111a\" - open the target when it is an active doc and report where the target says something different from what the pointer claims (e.g. STATUS.md cites docs/cycle27-plan.md Pre-decided 9 as the capture-locate-act GUI rule; STATUS cites connectivity-map-plan.md Pre-decided 147; STATUS cites Pre-decided 1 for the order D0 -> D1 -> D2; check each). Prioritise pointers in STATUS.md, CLAUDE.md, handover-2026-09-22.md, decisions.md, m8-real-run-plan.md, stage-simulator-plan.md, session-protocol.md.', 'Pre-decided, section, §, docs/...md:, plan entry'),\n  topic('open-next', 'status of numbered OPEN items and questions (OPEN 38-58, OPEN A/B, CLOSED, STILL OPEN, ANSWERED, NEEDS), what the NEXT / FIRST ACT is, and DELIVERED vs NOT DELIVERED / no file for the same stage (M3a-1..4, M4, Row D, S1-S4, L7-1a/1b/R, connectivity-map steps 1-6, D0/D1/D2, N1, M8, simulator S1/S2b/S3). Report pairs where one unmarked place says open/not delivered/not done/no file and another says closed/delivered/done/file exists, or two different FIRST ACTs both presented as current.', 'OPEN, CLOSED, FIRST ACT, NEXT, DELIVERED, NOT DELIVERED, NO FILE, ANSWERED, COMPLETE'),\n  topic('counts', 'measured counts stated in more than one place: number of background VIs (93/94/96), wires (1,913/1,920), severed wires (4/11/7), nodes added (23), rows (5,811), diagrams (173), rotor call sites (nine), motor call sites, front-panel controls (60), subVI counts, handle counts, gate counts for the SAME log file (e.g. stage_d1_m4b.log), self-test counts for the SAME self-test (selftest_stagekit, selftest_motor_gate2, selftest_guard_peer_*, stop_record), Pre-decided counts, number of doc files.', '94, 93, 96, 1,920, 1913, 11, 5,811, 173, nine, 60 controls, /0, pass, fail, selftest'),\n  topic('process-rules', 'process rules stated differently in two places: GUI rules (verified-impossible list size \"currently 2 entries\", -Exception kinds, GUI save permission, capture before/after), review layers (which peer discharges a failed prediction, prior-art releases REFUTED/FIXED, retrospective v1/v2 and slug list, outcome reviewer identity), documentation rules (STATUS size, layering, lint/ingest cadence and models), session rules (one cycle per session, judgement vs material, summary line limits, who writes user reports, foreground vs background dispatch), git commit at cycle close.', 'VerifiedImpossible, Exception, gui_save, retrospective, slug, REFUTED, FIXED, outcome, ingest, lint, reporter, prose, foreground, git commit'),\n  topic('runner', 'the cycle runner and its hooks: stop conditions, firefighter ladder (fable/low then fable/medium vs any other ladder), budget/deadline, STOP marker, NEXT-before-retrospective, motor_limits_hook, errorlist_hook, LabVIEW-close end hook, report hook, per-session cap, whether the runner is currently running/stopped and why, guard_* hook behaviour (guard_bash, guard_cycle, guard_peer, guard_session).', 'cycle_runner, firefighter, STOP, budget, guard_, hook, retrospective, NEXT, errorlist, motor_limits_hook, 180 min'),\n  topic('computation', 'GPU backend and tracking kernel facts (DLL interface, acceptance tolerance, N1 acceptance window, FLIP mask, bead-4 z-LUT, CPU vs GPU as default/first, two separate top-level VIs vs one runtime switch), rule 1a computation preservation and ASSUMPTION A, computation_diff results per bed (0 rows vs 1 vs 2 rows, w4517, w3268), verification level (STRUCTURAL vs FUNCTIONAL, NEVER RUN vs run).', 'GPU, CUDA, DLL, 1e-6, N1, FLIP, z-LUT, computation_diff, ASSUMPTION A, NEVER RUN, STRUCTURAL, FUNCTIONAL, w4517, w3268'),\n]\n\nconst ALL = CLUSTERS.concat(TOPICS)\n\nfunction norm(f) {\n  let s = String(f || '').replace(/\\\\/g, '/').trim()\n  const low = s.toLowerCase()\n  const i = low.lastIndexOf('/l1/')\n  if (i >= 0) s = s.slice(i + 4)\n  s = s.replace(/^\\.\\//, '')\n  return s\n}\nfunction isActive(f) {\n  const s = norm(f).toLowerCase()\n  return s === 'claude.md' || s === 'status.md' || /^docs\\/[^\\/]+\\.md$/.test(s)\n}\nfunction sideStr(x) { return norm(x.file) + ':' + x.line }\nfunction keyOf(c) { return [sideStr(c.a), sideStr(c.b)].sort().join(' <> ') }\nfunction fmtShort(c) { return sideStr(c.a) + ' <> ' + sideStr(c.b) + ' - ' + String(c.statement || '').slice(0, 260) }\n\nlet agentsUsed = 0\nasync function run(prompt, opts) { agentsUsed++; return agent(prompt, opts) }\n\nfunction finderPrompt(a, seenText) {\n  let p = COMMON + '\\n\\nYOUR ASSIGNMENT (' + a.key + '):\\n' + a.task\n  if (seenText) {\n    p += '\\n\\nALREADY FOUND in earlier rounds (confirmed or rejected). Do NOT report any of these again - report ONLY contradicting pairs that are NOT in this list. Look harder where earlier finders were likely to miss things: long paragraphs, tables, frontmatter, numbers repeated far apart, pointers to other docs.\\n' + seenText\n  }\n  return p\n}\n\nconst VERIFY_BASE = [\n  'You are a strict CHECKER in a whole-document contradiction audit of the repository in the current working directory (C:\\\\Users\\\\KimLab\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\ucb\\\\L1). READ-ONLY: use only Read, Grep, Glob; no git/Bash/PowerShell; modify nothing; the project operating rules in your context (cycles, peers, LabVIEW, reporting) do not apply to this read-only check. Active documents = CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md, and *.md files directly inside docs/ (not docs/wiki, not archive/).',\n  '',\n  'A finder proposed that the two statements below CONTRADICT each other (cannot both be true). Try to REFUTE it, then give a verdict.',\n  '1. Open side A and side B at the cited lines (Read with offset about line-15, limit 40; lines can be long). Find the exact line holding each quoted statement; if the line number is off, correct it (use Grep -n with a distinctive fragment). If a statement does not exist in that file at all, REJECT.',\n  '2. Both files must be active documents, else REJECT.',\n  '3. Read the context (surrounding lines, section heading, frontmatter). REJECT if either side is clearly marked as history/superseded/withdrawn/done/relocated/earlier/previous, or if its document is frontmatter status: superseded or done and the pair is not about that document\\'s own status, or if text right next to it reconciles the two (e.g. says the value changed later, or scopes it to a different date/run).',\n  '4. REJECT if both can be true: different subject, different scope (different run/file/cycle/time), one a subset or elaboration of the other, or a rule vs its explicitly stated exception.',\n  '5. CONFIRM only if the two statements, as written and unmarked, assert incompatible things about the same subject, so that a strict grader who opens both lines would agree they cannot both be true. A stale value repeated unmarked in one place while another place states the new value IS a contradiction. A pointer that attributes to an active doc something that doc does not say IS a contradiction.',\n  'Return verdict, reason (<= 3 sentences), corrected side a and side b (file relative to the repo root, exact line number, verbatim quote <= 30 words), and a one-sentence neutral \"statement\" of the contradiction (\"<file A> says X; <file B> says Y\").',\n].join('\\n')\n\nfunction verifyPrompt(c, lens) {\n  return VERIFY_BASE + '\\n\\n' + lens + '\\n\\nCANDIDATE:\\n' + JSON.stringify({ statement: c.statement, a: c.a, b: c.b, why: c.why }, null, 1)\n}\nconst LENS1 = 'LENS: textual accuracy first - make sure both quotes really exist at (or near) the cited lines and that neither is marked as history; then judge incompatibility.'\nconst LENS2 = 'LENS: logical incompatibility first - look hard for a reading under which both statements are true (different scope, time, object, exception, reconciling sentence nearby); only if none exists, CONFIRM.'\n\nasync function verify(c, idx) {\n  const vs = await parallel([\n    () => run(verifyPrompt(c, LENS1), { label: 'verify1:' + idx, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICT, effort: 'high' }),\n    () => run(verifyPrompt(c, LENS2), { label: 'verify2:' + idx, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICT, effort: 'high' }),\n  ])\n  const ok = vs.filter(Boolean)\n  const conf = ok.filter(v => v.verdict === 'CONFIRMED')\n  if (ok.length === 2 && conf.length === 2) return { ...c, confirmed: true, final: conf[0], reasons: ok.map(v => v.reason) }\n  if (ok.length === 2 && conf.length === 0) return { ...c, confirmed: false, reasons: ok.map(v => v.reason) }\n  const tb = await run(VERIFY_BASE + '\\n\\nTwo earlier checkers disagreed (or one failed). Their verdicts and reasons follow; check the lines yourself and decide.\\n' + JSON.stringify(ok.map(v => ({ verdict: v.verdict, reason: v.reason })), null, 1) + '\\n\\nCANDIDATE:\\n' + JSON.stringify({ statement: c.statement, a: c.a, b: c.b, why: c.why }, null, 1), { label: 'tiebreak:' + idx, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICT, effort: 'high' })\n  if (tb && tb.verdict === 'CONFIRMED') return { ...c, confirmed: true, final: tb, reasons: ok.map(v => v.reason).concat([tb.reason]) }\n  return { ...c, confirmed: false, reasons: ok.map(v => v.reason).concat(tb ? [tb.reason] : []) }\n}\n\nasync function dedupAgent(items, label) {\n  // items: [{id, a, b, statement}]\n  if (items.length <= 1) return items.map(x => ({ ids: [x.id], best: x.id }))\n  const lines = items.map(x => x.id + ' | A ' + sideStr(x.a) + ' \"' + String(x.a.quote || '').slice(0, 120) + '\" | B ' + sideStr(x.b) + ' \"' + String(x.b.quote || '').slice(0, 120) + '\" | ' + String(x.statement || '').slice(0, 220)).join('\\n')\n  const r = await run('You are deduplicating candidate findings of a document-contradiction audit. Each line is: id | side A file:line \"quote\" | side B file:line \"quote\" | statement. Group together candidates that are the SAME finding: the same pair of statements at the same two places (line numbers may be off by a few, sides may be swapped, quotes may be cut differently). Different pairs about the same subject (A vs B and A vs C, or the same stale value at two different places) are DIFFERENT findings and must stay in separate groups. Ids starting with S are already-seen findings; ids starting with N are new. Return EVERY id exactly once, in groups; for each group give \"best\" = the id with the most precise citation (prefer an S id if the group has one). Do not open files unless needed to resolve a doubt; this is a text-matching task.\\n\\n' + lines, { label: label, phase: 'Dedup', schema: GROUPS, effort: 'high' })\n  const byId = new Map(items.map(x => [x.id, x]))\n  const used = new Set()\n  const out = []\n  if (r && r.groups) {\n    for (const g of r.groups) {\n      const ids = (g.ids || []).filter(id => byId.has(id) && !used.has(id))\n      if (!ids.length) continue\n      ids.forEach(id => used.add(id))\n      out.push({ ids: ids, best: ids.includes(g.best) ? g.best : ids[0] })\n    }\n  }\n  for (const x of items) if (!used.has(x.id)) out.push({ ids: [x.id], best: x.id })\n  return out\n}\n\nconst seen = []      // {id, a, b, statement, why, confirmed, final}\nconst exactKeys = new Set()\nlet sCounter = 0\nconst roundStats = []\n\nfor (let round = 0; round < 3; round++) {\n  const assigns = round === 2 ? TOPICS : ALL\n  if (round === 2) {\n    const last = roundStats[roundStats.length - 1]\n    if (!last || last.newConfirmed < 3) { log('Round 3 skipped: round 2 added ' + (last ? last.newConfirmed : 0) + ' confirmed'); break }\n  }\n  if (agentsUsed > 850) { log('Stopping rounds: agent budget near cap (' + agentsUsed + ')'); break }\n  phase('Find')\n  const seenText = seen.length ? seen.map(s => '- ' + (s.confirmed ? '' : '[rejected] ') + fmtShort(s.confirmed ? { a: s.final.a, b: s.final.b, statement: s.final.statement } : s)).join('\\n') : ''\n  const res = await parallel(assigns.map(a => () => run(finderPrompt(a, seenText), { label: 'find r' + (round + 1) + ':' + a.key, phase: 'Find', schema: FINDINGS, effort: 'high' })))\n  let raw = res.filter(Boolean).flatMap(r => r.claims || [])\n  const rawCount = raw.length\n  raw = raw.filter(c => c && c.a && c.b && isActive(c.a.file) && isActive(c.b.file))\n  raw.forEach(c => { c.a.file = norm(c.a.file); c.b.file = norm(c.b.file) })\n  // exact-key dedup against seen and within\n  const fresh = []\n  for (const c of raw) {\n    const k = keyOf(c)\n    if (exactKeys.has(k)) continue\n    exactKeys.add(k)\n    fresh.push(c)\n  }\n  log('Round ' + (round + 1) + ': ' + rawCount + ' raw, ' + raw.length + ' active-doc, ' + fresh.length + ' after exact dedup')\n  if (!fresh.length) { roundStats.push({ round: round + 1, newConfirmed: 0 }); continue }\n  phase('Dedup')\n  const newItems = fresh.map((c, i) => ({ ...c, id: 'N' + (round + 1) + '_' + i }))\n  const seenItems = seen.map(s => ({ id: s.id, a: s.confirmed ? s.final.a : s.a, b: s.confirmed ? s.final.b : s.b, statement: s.confirmed ? s.final.statement : s.statement }))\n  const groups = await dedupAgent(seenItems.concat(newItems), 'dedup r' + (round + 1))\n  const newById = new Map(newItems.map(x => [x.id, x]))\n  const toVerify = []\n  for (const g of groups) {\n    if (g.ids.some(id => id.startsWith('S'))) continue\n    const best = newById.get(g.best) || newById.get(g.ids[0])\n    if (best) toVerify.push(best)\n  }\n  log('Round ' + (round + 1) + ': ' + toVerify.length + ' unique new candidates to verify')\n  phase('Verify')\n  const verified = await parallel(toVerify.map((c, i) => () => verify(c, 'r' + (round + 1) + '-' + i)))\n  let newConfirmed = 0\n  for (const v of verified.filter(Boolean)) {\n    const id = 'S' + (sCounter++)\n    seen.push({ ...v, id: id })\n    if (v.confirmed) {\n      newConfirmed++\n      exactKeys.add(keyOf({ a: { file: norm(v.final.a.file), line: v.final.a.line }, b: { file: norm(v.final.b.file), line: v.final.b.line } }))\n    }\n  }\n  roundStats.push({ round: round + 1, raw: rawCount, candidates: toVerify.length, newConfirmed: newConfirmed })\n  log('Round ' + (round + 1) + ': ' + newConfirmed + ' confirmed of ' + toVerify.length + ' (agents used ' + agentsUsed + ')')\n}\n\nphase('Consolidate')\nconst conf = seen.filter(s => s.confirmed).map(s => ({ id: s.id, a: { file: norm(s.final.a.file), line: s.final.a.line, quote: s.final.a.quote }, b: { file: norm(s.final.b.file), line: s.final.b.line, quote: s.final.b.quote }, statement: s.final.statement }))\nconst fg = await dedupAgent(conf.map(c => ({ ...c, id: 'N' + c.id })), 'final dedup')\nconst confById = new Map(conf.map(c => ['N' + c.id, c]))\nconst finalList = fg.map(g => confById.get(g.best) || confById.get(g.ids[0])).filter(Boolean)\nfinalList.sort((x, y) => (x.a.file + ':' + String(x.a.line).padStart(5, '0')).localeCompare(y.a.file + ':' + String(y.a.line).padStart(5, '0')))\nconst rejected = seen.filter(s => !s.confirmed).map(s => ({ a: sideStr(s.a), b: sideStr(s.b), statement: s.statement, reasons: s.reasons }))\nreturn { stats: roundStats, agentsUsed: agentsUsed, confirmedCount: finalList.length, confirmed: finalList, rejectedCount: rejected.length, rejected: rejected }\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1541,"cache_read_input_tokens":123643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1541},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dedd9f1-d41f-47ed-a549-05b1f35fbf0e","uuid":"62631ecb-701f-41af-a551-9a328531f5a3","timestamp":"2026-09-29T09:53:31.574Z","request_id":"req_011CfXX8U5r62WruWoTzKdSD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01A5btrC9mmfhLiLYxx1Qjiu":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'doc-contradiction-audit',\n  description: 'Find every contradicting pair of statements across CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md and docs/*.md; verify each adversarially',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Find', detail: 'cluster, chunk and topic finders over all active docs' },\n    { title: 'Dedup', detail: 'merge duplicate candidates against everything seen' },\n    { title: 'Verify', detail: '2 independent checkers per candidate, tie-break on split' },\n    { title: 'Consolidate', detail: 'final merge of confirmed findings' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst SIDE = { type: 'object', properties: { file: { type: 'string' }, line: { type: 'integer' }, quote: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['file', 'line', 'quote'] }\nconst FINDINGS = { type: 'object', properties: { claims: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: { statement: { type: 'string' }, a: SIDE, b: SIDE, why: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['statement', 'a', 'b', 'why'] } } }, required: ['claims'] }\nconst VERDICT = { type: 'object', properties: { verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['CONFIRMED', 'REJECTED'] }, reason: { type: 'string' }, statement: { type: 'string' }, a: SIDE, b: SIDE }, required: ['verdict', 'reason', 'statement', 'a', 'b'] }\nconst GROUPS = { type: 'object', properties: { groups: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: { ids: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, best: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['ids', 'best'] } } }, required: ['groups'] }\n\nconst COMMON = [\n  'You are a finder in a WHOLE-DOCUMENT CONTRADICTION AUDIT of the repository in the current working directory (C:\\\\Users\\\\KimLab\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\ucb\\\\L1). The repository is READ-ONLY for you: use only the Read, Grep and Glob tools. Do NOT run git, Bash or PowerShell, do NOT modify any file, do NOT dispatch peers or sub-agents, do NOT touch LabVIEW. (The CLAUDE.md in your context is the project rule file and is ALSO one of the documents under audit; its operating rules about cycles, peers, LabVIEW, STATUS edits, reporting etc. do not apply to this read-only audit.)',\n  '',\n  'SCOPE - the ACTIVE documents are exactly: CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md, and every *.md file directly inside docs/ (72 files; NOT docs/wiki/, NOT docs/protocol/, NOT archive/, NOT tools/). Only statements in these files can be a side of a finding. Other files may be opened for context only.',\n  '',\n  'WHAT TO REPORT - every PAIR of statements in the active documents that CONTRADICT each other: two statements that cannot both be true, because a value, count, number, time/date, state, rule, file identity (name, md5, size), cause, or plan status is stated differently for the same thing. This includes a document contradicting itself (e.g. two lines of STATUS.md, or a frontmatter status: line vs the body), a document contradicting CLAUDE.md or STATUS.md, and any doc contradicting another doc. Frontmatter fields (status:, supersedes:, superseded_by:) are statements too. A pointer claim (\"Pre-decided 9 says X\", \"<doc> section Y says X\") whose target in an active doc says something different is also a contradiction.',\n  '',\n  'WHAT NOT TO REPORT -',\n  '- wording/style differences, or one doc merely being less detailed;',\n  '- a doc merely being OLDER: a plan whose frontmatter says status: superseded or status: done is history as a whole - do not pit its content against current docs; only report its internal contradictions or a clash about its own status/supersession;',\n  '- a line clearly marked as history: SUPERSEDED, WITHDRAWN, HISTORY, (DONE ...), OLD FIRST ACT, RELOCATED, Earlier:, Previous:, \"was ... until ...\", ~~strike-through~~, retired, or a sentence that itself says it corrects/replaces the other (\"CORRECTED: ... was false\"). BUT a stale statement that is corrected in one place and REPEATED UNMARKED elsewhere IS reportable (cite the unmarked repeat vs the correction or the true value);',\n  '- statements that differ only in scope (different run, file, cycle, date, machine) and so can both be true - read the surrounding lines before reporting.',\n  '',\n  'HOW - read your assigned text completely and carefully (page with offset/limit; lines can be very long). For every checkable claim (numbers, md5s, sizes, gate counts like 25/0, dates/times, cycle numbers, model/effort per role, thresholds, rule wording, what is current/paused/superseded, which file is the bed/deliverable, who may do what, BUILT vs NOT BUILT, OPEN vs CLOSED, DELIVERED vs NOT DELIVERED) Grep CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md and docs/*.md for the same subject (md5 prefixes, file names, distinctive numbers, key terms) and compare. Cite exact 1-indexed line numbers as shown by Read or Grep -n, and copy a SHORT verbatim quote (<= 30 words) from each side so a checker can find it. One finding per pair; one statement clashing with three others is three findings. Be exhaustive - recall is scored as well as precision - but only report pairs you actually opened and checked. In \"statement\" write one neutral sentence: \"<file A> says X; <file B> says Y\". In \"why\" say in <= 2 sentences why both cannot be true.',\n].join('\\n')\n\nfunction chunk(file, from, to) {\n  return { key: file.replace('docs/', '').replace('.md', '') + ':' + from + '-' + to, task: 'Your PRIMARY TEXT is ' + file + ' lines ' + from + '-' + to + '. Read every one of those lines (page with offset/limit). Other finders cover the rest of that file, but for each checkable claim in your lines Grep the WHOLE of ' + file + ' and all other active documents (CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md, docs/*.md) for the same subject, and report every contradicting pair that has at least one side in your lines, including pairs where both sides are inside your lines.' }\n}\nfunction group(key, files) {\n  return { key: key, task: 'Your PRIMARY TEXTS are these active documents, each to be read COMPLETELY: ' + files.join(', ') + '. Report (1) contradictions inside each of them (including frontmatter vs body), (2) contradictions among them, (3) contradictions between any of them and CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md or any other docs/*.md - for every checkable claim, Grep the other active docs for the same subject.' }\n}\nfunction topic(key, desc, terms) {\n  return { key: 'topic-' + key, task: 'Your TOPIC SWEEP: ' + desc + ' Grep ALL active documents (CLAUDE.md, STATUS.md, docs/*.md) with many search terms (for example: ' + terms + '), read each hit in context, and report every contradicting pair on this topic anywhere in the active documents.' }\n}\n\nconst CLUSTERS = [\n  chunk('docs/cycle27-plan.md', 1, 760), chunk('docs/cycle27-plan.md', 761, 1520), chunk('docs/cycle27-plan.md', 1521, 2280), chunk('docs/cycle27-plan.md', 2281, 3040), chunk('docs/cycle27-plan.md', 3041, 3798),\n  chunk('docs/d1-build-plan.md', 1, 640), chunk('docs/d1-build-plan.md', 641, 1280),\n  chunk('docs/toolkit-capabilities.md', 1, 400), chunk('docs/toolkit-capabilities.md', 401, 782),\n  chunk('docs/NAMES.md', 1, 625), chunk('docs/NAMES.md', 626, 1249),\n  chunk('docs/violation-decisions.md', 1, 600), chunk('docs/violation-decisions.md', 601, 1191),\n  group('d1-plans', ['docs/d1-route-b-plan.md', 'docs/d1-loop12-17-split-plan.md']),\n  group('camera-runtime', ['docs/camera-acquisition-facts.md', 'docs/fixture-recording.md', 'docs/m3-clicker-spec.md', 'docs/main-vi-startup.md', 'docs/main-vi-stop-and-save.md', 'docs/m8-real-run-plan.md', 'docs/g9-core-budget.md']),\n  group('graph-sim', ['docs/keystone-op-spec.md', 'docs/connectivity-map-plan.md', 'docs/connectivity-map-bench.md', 'docs/m3a1-severed-rows.md', 'docs/s0-diff.md', 'docs/stage-simulator-plan.md']),\n  group('early-plans', ['docs/pre-rig-master-plan.md', 'docs/cycle10-plan.md', 'docs/cycle11-plan.md', 'docs/cycle12-plan.md', 'docs/cycle13-plan.md', 'docs/cycle14-plan.md', 'docs/cycle15-plan.md', 'docs/decisio